      "headline": "Fireworks AI |  Carnegie Mellon University |  University of Waterloo",
      "about": "For me, life is an adventure, and playing sports makes it all the more adventurous. As a kid, it was the cerebral sport of Chess that most appealed to me and my faculties. As a passionate aficionado of this conflict where the contenders are sovereigns of two feudal monarchies, I progressed through several state and national level competitions.\n\nOne of the competitions was held at a rural government-aided school. The dark, velvety green patch of seepage on the dormitory wall reminded me of the dense Amazonian jungles. Sunlight filtered through the broken begrimed windows, and the walls bore patterns of peeling plaster and cobwebs. Standing there, I thought, 'How on earth do students study here?’\n\nOn our way back, my twin and I were discussing the horrendous status of schools in rural India. Suddenly a bigger battle came into view, one of helping elevate the infrastructure of institutions all over rural India.\n\nAfter much pondering and brainstorming of ideas, the moment of epiphany arrived. We collaborated on an idea for the social technology platform💡“Vhelpconnect\" and prototyped a website that allows institutions in need, corporations, and volunteers to register and connect with each other in order to improve the distribution of charitable resources as acts of corporate social responsibility (CSR). This endeavor has strengthened my love for computer science, a great means of transformation. Thus, began my journey in the field of technology.\n\n📍Website: http://vhelpconnect.org/ \n(Edit: Hold on to your virtual hats. The website has been taken down, i.e., went on a vacation—currently soaking up some digital sun and sipping on 404 errors 🏝️🚫)",
